<Template>
  <!-- One deck's stem strip: four rows of Mixxx 2.6's real per-stem controls,
       instantiated from waveform.xml, which has already set `channel`.

       The whole group hangs off [ChannelN],stem_count, and that one connection
       is what makes this file safe to ship to a box running 2.5.6. On 2.6
       stem_count is a read-only control the engine writes when a track with a
       manifest is loaded, so the strip appears for stem tracks and for nothing
       else. On 2.5.6 there is no stem engine and no such control, so the skin
       parser conjures it at zero, nothing ever writes it, and the strip is
       hidden from the moment it is built and stays hidden for ever. The
       property connection reads the control once in its constructor, so this
       is not a flicker that settles: the group is never shown at all.

       That is the same mechanism that cost this project four dead buttons,
       the parser inventing a control nobody writes, turned round to point the
       other way. A control that reads zero for ever makes a button that lies;
       it also makes a container that stays shut.

       RequiresStem is 2.6's own gate, and it is here for the third case: a 2.6
       built without __STEM__ skips this group at parse time, so not even the
       phantom controls are created. 2.5.6 does not know the element and ignores
       it, which is why it cannot serve as the version test on its own.

       Four rows, in slot order, top to bottom. That order is not this skin's
       to choose and it is not alphabetical: the renderer in the DDJ-1000
       repository writes rekordbox's own four-stem PartLayout, DRUMS, VOCAL,
       INST, BASS, so that slots 1 to 3 sit under the three ACTIVE PART buttons
       the unit has. Keeping the rows in the same order means the three buttons
       to the left of this strip, DRUMS VOCAL INST, stand beside the three rows
       they name, and BASS, the slot with no button, is the one left over at the
       bottom. The words themselves still come out of the file. -->
  <WidgetGroup>
    <ObjectName>StemStrip</ObjectName>
    <RequiresStem>true</RequiresStem>
    <Layout>vertical</Layout>
    <Size>244f,0me</Size>
    <Children>
      <Template src="skin:stem_channel.xml">
        <SetVariable name="stem">1</SetVariable>
      </Template>
      <Template src="skin:stem_channel.xml">
        <SetVariable name="stem">2</SetVariable>
      </Template>
      <Template src="skin:stem_channel.xml">
        <SetVariable name="stem">3</SetVariable>
      </Template>
      <Template src="skin:stem_channel.xml">
        <SetVariable name="stem">4</SetVariable>
      </Template>
    </Children>
    <Connection>
      <ConfigKey>[Channel<Variable name="channel"/>],stem_count</ConfigKey>
      <BindProperty>visible</BindProperty>
    </Connection>
  </WidgetGroup>
</Template>
